Douglas Mendum wrote:

> In the weapon spoilers it says that Cleaver does +d3 to hit and +d6
> damage. What does this actually mean?

+dX means "add a random number from 1 to X".

If you hit with Cleaver, you'll do an additional 1-6 points of damage over
a regular battle axe.  To determine if you hit, a "die" is rolled, and if
the result is above a particular number you hit.  With Cleaver, when this
die is rolled 1-3 is added to the result.

